  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Night Studio Toy Box",
    "overview": "A navy night lit by periwinkle stage light, where a cast of glossy 3D toys and big, quiet DM Sans type act out an idea. The system is made for the 1920 × 1080 frame, not a scrolling page: one statement at a time, set large on an open field, with a character doing something next to it. Every visual is a pure function of time. Stills such as the thumbnail are frames of the same world, so they borrow its motion language (arcs, squash, onion skins, time stamps) instead of freezing a title over a paused frame.\n\nThe world has two palettes: the dark navy night, and a light ice day. It switches between them only through a circular wipe that opens from a point, usually where the hero lands. Depth comes from light, not from boxes: drifting blurred glows, glows that bleed off periwinkle elements, and the gloss on the toys. The editor's tools carry the craft story: a thin selection box with square handles and a pointer cursor turn a word into something that has just been made.\n\nThe cut is unbranded by design. Nothing in the visual system identifies a client: no logo, wordmark, URL or trust badge. The cast is the face of the work.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Navy night (#050817 to #070B22) with periwinkle glows; light ice (#F5F7FF) as the second palette, reached only by a circular wipe.",
      "DM Sans throughout, carried by weight contrast: Regular 400 for the line, Bold 700 for the one word that matters.",
      "The selection box with square handles and the pointer cursor as the signature devices.",
      "A cast of four glossy toy blobs (periwinkle hero with antenna, mint in a hard hat, coral in glasses, yellow in a headset).",
      "Motion by springs, parabolic hops and damped landing squash; never linear."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Two Nights Rule",
        "body": "The world has exactly two grounds, the navy night and the ice day. A scene changes ground only through a circular wipe that grows from a point (soft edge 30 px, inOutCubic, to 2300 px radius); never a cut or a crossfade between palettes.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Warmth Lives in the Toys Rule",
        "body": "Coral, yellow, orange and blush belong to the cast's materials. Type, UI and background stay in the periwinkle and mint family.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Weight Contrast Rule",
        "body": "A line is Regular 400; one word, at most two, is Bold 700. Never a full line in Bold, never a size jump inside a line.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Measurement Rule",
        "body": "Small type in the frame is a measurement (time stamps) or a credit, set in tabular figures beside what it measures. It never sits above a headline as a category label.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Glow Not Slab Rule",
        "body": "Every shadow is blurred and pulled in with negative spread, or is a coloured glow; edges are drawn with inset hairlines (1 to 2px), not outer borders.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep every headline line in DM Sans 400 and set the one word that matters in 700 white, inside the selection box when it is the hero word.",
      "**Do** change ground only by a circular wipe between the navy night and the ice day.",
      "**Do** flip editor devices for the light palette: cursor ink with a white outline, accents in periwinkle-deep (#4A5BD0), text in ink (#0D1020).",
      "**Do** build depth from glows and the toys' gloss; draw edges as 1 to 2px inset hairlines.",
      "**Do** move everything on springs, hops and damped squash, with toys looking where they are going.",
      "**Do** set time stamps in 500 tabular figures in periwinkle-light, next to what they measure."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** put any client name, logo, wordmark, URL, trust badge or client figure on the portfolio cut or its promo surfaces.",
      "**Don't** use hard, offset, unblurred shadows; every shadow is a soft lift or a coloured glow.",
      "**Don't** set a small label or kicker above a headline; supporting lines go below it.",
      "**Don't** give type, UI or backgrounds the toys' warm colours (coral, yellow, orange).",
      "**Don't** use Inter or Schibsted Grotesk for the film's voice; they are scoped to in-film product UI and outline stacks.",
      "**Don't** round the selection box's corners or handles beyond 2px.",
      "**Don't** draw motion paths, tick marks, dotted trails, stage-light rings or scattered dust dots on stills; the ghosts carry the motion."
    ]
  }
